[QA 1] The paper presents efficient FPGA implementations of the tweakable enciphering schemes FAST and AEZ, demonstrating that FAST outperforms other disk encryption schemes, making it a strong candidate for future disk encryption standards and hardware implementations. | The key contribution of the paper "Fast Low Level Disk Encryption Using FPGAs" is that it presents efficient FPGA implementations of the FAST and AEZ tweakable enciphering schemes, which are promising candidates for low-level disk encryption, and shows that the FAST implementations outperform the IEEE standards XCB and EME2 as well as the AEZ implementation in terms of throughput and area requirements, making FAST a strong contender for adoption by disk manufacturers and standardization bodies.
